# Fair CRM development standard is mandatory

Canonical sources:

- `kyrox-platform/projects/fair-crm/DEVELOPMENT_STANDARD.md`
- `kyrox-platform/projects/fair-crm/FEATURE_APPLICABILITY_STANDARD.md`
- `kyrox-platform/projects/fair-crm/QUALITY_GATE_STANDARD.md`

Before changing product code for a new module, feature, CRUD flow, service, worker, scheduled job, adapter, permission, route, migration, backend behavior or frontend UI:

1. Read the canonical development standard.
2. Classify the Feature Profile and applicability before implementation.
3. Complete Gate 0 / Delivery Contract for all applicable fields.
4. Mark every delivery area as REQUIRED or N/A; every N/A needs a concrete architectural reason.
5. Do not invent CRUD permissions, frontend pages, menus or role checks for backend-only/internal features merely to satisfy a generic checklist.
6. Apply ADR-009 ownership and Tier classification rules.
7. Decide permission scope for every new permission before implementation.
8. For a new material feature, create/update the machine-readable `.kyrox/features/<feature-id>.json` contract so CI can validate applicability and detectable material changes.
9. Follow the gate order; do not jump directly from request to API/page code.
10. Backend truth, tenant isolation and authorization must exist before UI is accepted.
11. UI navigation, routes and actions must reflect effective permissions; backend authorization remains mandatory.
12. Real JWT + organization + Core authorization + Fair CRM API + UI acceptance is required only where runtime authorization is applicable. Mock/bypass/build-only evidence is insufficient for those paths.
13. Frontend UI changes also require `kyrox-platform/projects/fair-crm/frontend/FRONTEND_UI_MASTER_STANDARD.md`.
14. Permission changes also require `kyrox-platform/projects/fair-crm/PERMISSION_SCOPE_GOVERNANCE.md`.
15. Quality reporting must distinguish strict green from zero-new-regression PASS with known debt. Existing baselines may shrink only; never add a newly introduced failure to make CI green.

Hard stop conditions include ambiguous requirements, guessed applicability, unexplained N/A gates, guessed permission scope, missing tenant scoping, hard-coded authenticated organization IDs, missing route/action permission guards where UI is applicable, invented UI/CRUD for non-user-facing services, duplicated UI primitives, stale-runtime acceptance, unintended real-runtime 401/403/500, or growth of a known-failure/quality-debt baseline.

Do not duplicate the canonical Markdown standards inside this repository. Update `kyrox-platform` when the rule changes.
